# Force LF line endings on files that run as shell scripts on Linux (the
# JUSUF cluster, or any Linux training machine), regardless of this repo's
# core.autocrlf setting on a given Windows checkout. CRLF in a script with a
# #!/bin/bash shebang breaks on Linux with "bad interpreter: ... no such
# file or directory" or "$'\r': command not found" -- a real, easy-to-hit
# runtime error the moment a Windows-checked-out .sbatch file is copied
# straight to the cluster. Without this, Windows' core.autocrlf=true
# (confirmed set on this machine) converts these back to CRLF on every
# checkout, silently reintroducing the bug after any git operation.
*.sbatch text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
